<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernesto Geisel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a>–<a href="/years/1996">1996</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernesto Geisel was a Brazilian army general who served as president from 1974 to 1979, the fourth of the military dictatorship. He began a slow, controlled political opening, the distensão, eased censorship and in 1978 revoked the repressive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/institutional-act-number-five">Institutional Act Number Five</a>. He pursued state-led industrial projects and nuclear power. He chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joao-figueiredo">João Figueiredo</a> as his successor, who completed the move back towards civilian rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernesto-geisel.jpg" alt="Ernesto Geisel" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federal Government of Brazil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foto_oficial_de_Ernesto_Geisel_(corre%C3%A7%C3%A3o_de_cor)_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
